    "title": "Four Chords, One Hand",
    "summary": "Major, minor, diminished and augmented sit under one hand with the root held still — the whole quality system is two fingers, moved one fret at a time.",
    "tags": ["triads", "chords", "fretboard"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Major, minor, diminished and augmented are not four different chords to learn. They are one shape, with the root held still and two fingers moved a fret at a time, into four different chords."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
