    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The third and the fifth are two separate voices, and each moves by one fret entirely on its own: the third is either "
        },
        {
          "text": "3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "text": "b3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; the fifth is "
        },
        {
          "text": "b5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", or "
        },
        {
          "text": "#5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Which note in the grip is which depends only on the inversion — the same two rules from earlier in this chapter, side by side: the third is the middle note in root position, the bass in first inversion, the top in second; the fifth is the top note in root position, the middle in first inversion, the bass in second."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This closes a loop from the very start of the pathway. A triad is two stacked thirds, and a third is either "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " semitones or "
        },
        {
          "text": "3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — two slots, two choices, four combinations: "
        },
        {
          "text": "4+3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is major, "
        },
        {
          "text": "3+4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is minor, "
        },
        {
          "text": "3+3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is diminished, "
        },
        {
          "text": "4+4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is augmented. That's the complete list, and it's complete for a reason rather than by convention. The two leftover combinations don't make new chords: "
        },
        {
          "text": "1 b3 #5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " over "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is "
        },
        {
          "text": "C Eb G#",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", which is just "
        },
        {
          "text": "Ab",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " major with "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " in the bass — "
        },
        {
          "text": "Ab/C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". And "
        },
        {
          "text": "1 3 b5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " ("
        },
        {
          "text": "C E Gb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ") doesn't stack in thirds at all; it has no triad name."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The four qualities share a bass fret in root position on three of the four sets: strings 1-2-3 at fret 5, strings 2-3-4 at fret 10, strings 4-5-6 at fret 8. Not on strings 3-4-5, where "
        },
        {
          "text": "Cdim",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " can't sit at fret 3 — "
        },
        {
          "text": "the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Gb",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " it needs falls a semitone below the open "
        },
        {
          "text": "G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " string"
        },
        {
          "text": " — and is stranded at "
        },
        {
          "text": "x 15 13 11 x x",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " instead."
        }
      ]
